WEBVTT

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:00.470
So this is how it ends.

00:02:00.470 --> 00:02:03.340
I believe I warned you.

00:02:03.340 --> 00:02:06.910
Symbol might not be as generous
as you believed them to be.

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:08.550
With the experiments over,

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:14.520
the fate of a small nation such
as Belgistan is immaterial.

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:17.820
While we may be a small country,
Belgistan is sovereign nation!

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:21.190
Underestimate it, and a rude
awakening may be in store!

00:02:21.190 --> 00:02:24.630
Sovereign, I humbly
accept your advice.

00:02:25.330 --> 00:02:30.560
It would seem that you still do not
fully comprehend our power.

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:33.900
Of course, it can't be helped.

00:02:33.900 --> 00:02:39.100
You believed Symbol couldn't
possibly afford to cut you off.

00:02:39.640 --> 00:02:41.010
If push comes to shove,

00:02:41.010 --> 00:02:44.150
you are willing to make public
all that took place here

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:47.520
in order to take us down
along with you.

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:48.880
Forgive me if I am mistaken.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:51.690
Unfortunately for you,

00:02:51.690 --> 00:02:57.530
we are not able to sit idle while
someone conspires against us.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:01.770
You seem to understand
better now.

00:03:01.770 --> 00:03:02.730
You didn't...

00:03:02.730 --> 00:03:07.810
Yes, just as we drew up the script
for the first act of this incident,

00:03:07.810 --> 00:03:12.240
we also put together this
coup d'état plot twist.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:16.710
We have been involved in the
politics of this nation

00:03:16.710 --> 00:03:19.820
for far, far longer than
you imagined.

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:22.750
Yes, for a very long time.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:26.560
Not just here, in the other nations
around you as well.

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:27.930
Lies!

00:03:27.930 --> 00:03:29.490
Oh, yes.

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:33.460
That message you entrusted to be
released to the mass media...

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:36.800
I realize how rude this is, but
we had it eliminated.

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:40.600
You see, we are a tremendously
shy group of people.

00:03:40.600 --> 00:03:44.900
We can't rest unless everything
about us is swept clean.

00:03:47.650 --> 00:03:50.180
According to reports coming
out of Belgistan,

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:52.650
a coup d'état took place early
this morning before dawn.

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:55.490
It has been reported that
the rebel forces

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:57.980
arrested the de facto leader of
Belgistan, Colonel Stilbanov...

00:03:59.620 --> 00:04:02.330
A formal request for a ceasefire
was delivered to the UN

00:04:02.330 --> 00:04:04.690
by the coup forces today at noon.

00:04:05.760 --> 00:04:09.270
With Belgistan making an official
request for a ceasefire,

00:04:09.270 --> 00:04:12.670
the focus is now on the allies'
reaction to this latest event.

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:14.770
Belgistan has made it clear

00:04:14.770 --> 00:04:15.910
the allies must withdraw before
any further negotiations.

00:04:15.910 --> 00:04:17.810
Yes, there's a lot of commotion at
the UN with this ceasefire.
the allies must withdraw before
any further negotiations.

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:21.910
Yes, there's a lot of commotion at
the UN with this ceasefire.
And it appears that unless this
condition is met, Belgistan,

00:04:21.910 --> 00:04:24.950
An inspection team is being put
together as we speak.
along with her neighbors, may
resort to military action.

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:25.950
An inspection team is being put
together as we speak.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:28.850
An inspection team? Why now?

00:04:28.850 --> 00:04:30.320
It's America.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:36.530
The Americans are lobbying the
UN to inspect the explosion site.

00:04:36.530 --> 00:04:39.620
But this is just a smoke screen.

00:04:40.700 --> 00:04:42.630
They're after the Tactical Armor.

00:04:42.630 --> 00:04:45.470
That's the amazing thing about
the United States.

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:49.870
Apparently, they are captivated
with the TA's possibilities.

00:04:49.870 --> 00:04:53.910
I've learned of orders
to local US forces

00:04:53.910 --> 00:04:56.950
to covertly collect any and all
intelligence regarding the TA's.

00:04:56.950 --> 00:05:02.090
Japan's petty officials are only
interested in protecting their jobs.

00:05:02.090 --> 00:05:06.020
Washington is far more perceptive
about how things are.

00:05:06.920 --> 00:05:10.730
But since the TA's can't claim any
noteworthy successes for now,

00:05:10.730 --> 00:05:15.130
we're not ready to show them off
to the international community.

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:18.160
In any case, the timing
is all wrong.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:20.500
Get out of there as soon
as you can.

00:05:21.670 --> 00:05:25.440
We might have problems with
the sample we secured.

00:05:26.140 --> 00:05:28.210
Is something bothering you?

00:05:28.210 --> 00:05:30.850
That sample is very
important to us, but

00:05:30.850 --> 00:05:35.950
don't you think it's as important
to them as Mile One is to us?

00:05:36.490 --> 00:05:37.920
No doubt.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:38.950
I was afraid of that.

00:05:41.190 --> 00:05:46.000
We are to prioritize the pullout of
our forces, General Dole.

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:47.500
I understand.

00:05:47.500 --> 00:05:50.600
But we need to pull back our
forces on the double

00:05:50.600 --> 00:05:53.370
so we can get the ceasefire
negotiations going.

00:05:54.510 --> 00:05:58.000
Yes, I will talk to the Japanese
government about this.

00:05:58.680 --> 00:06:01.840
The SSDF's pullout is going
to have to wait.

00:06:10.520 --> 00:06:14.860
We should begin investigating
the Japanese Fakes today.

00:06:14.860 --> 00:06:17.620
Let the Council know.

00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:20.590
Miharu?

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:23.170
It's a directive from F.

00:06:23.170 --> 00:06:28.230
The relationship between the
Japanese invitator and Miharu
must be made clear.

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:31.610
And that's why the
Church of Akura.

00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:33.740
But...

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:36.610
Yes, we need to investigate
that as well.

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:40.610
Why did Miharu display such
a strong interest?

00:06:41.320 --> 00:06:44.050
Finding that out will...

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:54.960
This just in.

00:06:56.030 --> 00:06:59.340
An emergency session of the UN
Security Council has accepted
Belgistan's request

00:06:59.340 --> 00:07:01.510
and the resolution for the
withdrawal of multinational forces

00:07:01.510 --> 00:07:05.410
from Belgistan within twenty-four
hours has been approved.

00:07:05.910 --> 00:07:10.480
Key to the passage of the
resolution was the guidance by
EU member states,

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:13.550
a group deeply concerned over the
nature of the explosion,

00:07:13.550 --> 00:07:16.080
and also pressing for a wider
comprehensive...

00:07:17.990 --> 00:07:20.320
Six flights? That's impossible!

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:23.960
This place will be nuts for the next
ten hours with the US pullout!

00:07:23.960 --> 00:07:29.260
The first of the inspectors will be
arriving in about twenty hours.

00:07:29.900 --> 00:07:33.460
We need to get the TA forces
out before then.

00:07:33.970 --> 00:07:36.500
The best I can do is four.
That's all.

00:07:37.370 --> 00:07:39.870
Yes, we'll have the C&C vehicle
make it back on its own.

00:07:40.640 --> 00:07:42.280
That's right, we'll drive it back.

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:44.350
What we can't leave without
is the combat records,

00:07:44.350 --> 00:07:47.650
and the updates to the system
that have been done.

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:51.260
If all else fails, as long as we can
get that and the TA's back,

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:54.790
we'll be able to salvage something
worthwhile from this deployment.

00:07:54.790 --> 00:07:57.390
Give us an hour and we'll
be ready to go!

00:07:57.390 --> 00:07:58.490
One hour...

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:01.430
That'll be just enough time
to make it to the flight.

00:08:01.430 --> 00:08:04.230
But that's if nothing breaks down
between now and then!

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:06.270
We'll deal with that as it happens.

00:08:06.270 --> 00:08:08.830
I'll have the flights back
prepared separately.

00:08:09.470 --> 00:08:11.210
Separately?

00:08:11.210 --> 00:08:12.730
Separate flights?

00:08:13.610 --> 00:08:17.640
Wow, red carpet accommodations
courtesy of Gowa, I guess!

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:20.380
This has nothing to do with Gowa!

00:08:20.380 --> 00:08:23.380
We're accelerating our pullout on
orders from our government!

00:08:24.050 --> 00:08:26.820
We will depart one hour from now.

00:08:26.820 --> 00:08:29.360
Major Takayama will assume
command after we leave!

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:31.130
Check systems flow.

00:08:31.130 --> 00:08:36.300
Leg drive system, triple data bus,
no irregularities reported.

00:08:36.300 --> 00:08:38.890
Captain Gowa, please
check the data.

00:08:40.070 --> 00:08:43.340
Leg hard points, confirmed
power cut off.

00:08:43.340 --> 00:08:46.310
Primary power output, six percent.

00:08:46.310 --> 00:08:48.800
Shutting down CBL systems
in the upper arms.

00:08:49.910 --> 00:08:52.680
Shut down individual
feedback loops.

00:08:52.680 --> 00:08:55.290
Shutting down leg feedback loops.

00:08:55.290 --> 00:08:57.010
Okay, it's all right.

00:08:57.650 --> 00:08:59.120
Oh, I screwed up!

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:02.690
I didn't have to shut off the
feed forwarding circuits.

00:09:02.690 --> 00:09:04.060
Don't worry about it.

00:09:04.060 --> 00:09:09.130
We need to update most of the
system once we get back.

00:09:09.130 --> 00:09:12.370
I suppose. It's not as if
it will malfunction.

00:09:12.370 --> 00:09:13.430
Lieutenant Murai!

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:17.270
We can't rely on slings alone?

00:09:17.270 --> 00:09:18.710
I knew it.

00:09:18.710 --> 00:09:21.110
It's 270km to the depot.

00:09:21.110 --> 00:09:24.720
Helicopter turbine engines don't
work well in high temperatures.

00:09:24.720 --> 00:09:25.720
On top of that, we've got
sand blowing about.

00:09:25.720 --> 00:09:27.650
Final check procedure.
On top of that, we've got
sand blowing about.

00:09:27.650 --> 00:09:29.950
Go ahead and shut down the
mainframe systems.
You can't expect it to
do everything.

00:09:29.950 --> 00:09:30.350
Go ahead and shut down the
mainframe systems.

00:09:34.420 --> 00:09:37.880
Major, I've completed all check
procedures for Unit 1.

00:09:38.630 --> 00:09:40.890
Wow, you're fast!

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:44.290
I don't make idle chitchat
while I am working.

00:09:49.010 --> 00:09:52.000
Well, this is work we're not
used to. Can't be helped.

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:56.380
I would like to start working
on Captain Ataka's TA.

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:59.720
Well, Captain Ataka is at the
administration center.

00:09:59.720 --> 00:10:01.210
Gowa's...

00:10:03.250 --> 00:10:05.120
There was a request from
Mr. Kiyoharu.

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:07.720
While we did secure
helicopter transportation,

00:10:07.720 --> 00:10:09.530
with the situation being as it is,

00:10:09.530 --> 00:10:13.790
some unscrupulous characters
keep meddling with our flights.

00:10:15.230 --> 00:10:17.940
The Captain couldn't get through
the door fast enough.

00:10:17.940 --> 00:10:20.870
She was overjoyed at getting out
of doing all this mundane work.

00:10:24.010 --> 00:10:27.340
Well, it seems we need to get her
back here as soon as we can.

00:10:28.210 --> 00:10:29.340
Captain Gowa!

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:32.620
Yes, Sir.

00:10:32.620 --> 00:10:35.790
Go to the administration center,
and have Captain Ataka return.

00:10:35.790 --> 00:10:36.780
Yes, Sir.

00:10:38.920 --> 00:10:42.650
I'll go to the center, and request
she return at once.

00:10:47.970 --> 00:10:51.840
Before Captain Gowa was like
sand that crumbles away,

00:10:51.840 --> 00:10:55.010
showing little resistance.

00:10:55.010 --> 00:10:58.240
But now, he's like a delicate and
transparent crystal glass.

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:03.410
He's someone who comes across
as fragile, about to break apart.

00:11:03.410 --> 00:11:06.810
Seems like Captain Gowa's
heart isn't with us right now.

00:11:09.190 --> 00:11:13.020
But I wonder why he did
those crazy things?

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:16.190
Didn't he realize what kind of
danger he was putting us in?

00:11:19.700 --> 00:11:23.860
It was a mistake from the start to
have a civilian with us.

00:11:27.970 --> 00:11:30.810
I can't believe it! Why?!

00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:31.340
Well...

00:11:31.340 --> 00:11:35.710
Geez! Your brother asked me to
come here, but just as we figured,

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:39.240
our flight was rescheduled
without us knowing it!

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:42.320
Okay, okay. I understand.

00:11:42.320 --> 00:11:47.190
But our flight schedule was made
up by your commander, Mr. Dole.
Do you know?

00:11:47.720 --> 00:11:52.060
Then I hope we'll be back, and talk
with your commander again.

00:11:54.300 --> 00:11:57.600
Just look at him once I mention
the name of some higher up.

00:11:58.370 --> 00:11:59.890
So, what did you want with me?

00:12:01.240 --> 00:12:05.210
Major Takayama requests that you
return to work on the TA's

00:12:05.210 --> 00:12:06.700
in preparations for transport.

00:12:07.610 --> 00:12:10.410
I'll be right with you. Do as much
as you can without me, okay?

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:11.900
Would you, Yushiro?

00:12:14.890 --> 00:12:19.020
It was feared that Akura Church,
which is carved in stone,
might be damaged,

00:12:19.020 --> 00:12:23.790
but it appears that it remained
unharmed during this conflict.

00:12:46.950 --> 00:12:49.320
There was no sign of
him at the barracks.

00:12:49.320 --> 00:12:50.850
What about at his brothers' place?

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:56.050
No, both of them were surprised to
hear that he had gone missing.

00:12:58.860 --> 00:13:03.070
What if we don't find him by
the time we take off?

00:13:03.070 --> 00:13:05.090
Then we would delay our
departure!

00:13:05.900 --> 00:13:08.740
I made a promise to the captain,

00:13:08.740 --> 00:13:11.710
that I would get him back to Japan
no matter what happens.

00:13:16.810 --> 00:13:18.050
I know where he is!

00:13:18.050 --> 00:13:21.250
Yushiro headed to the stone
carved Church of Akura.

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:22.510
Stone carved church?

00:13:23.490 --> 00:13:25.750
It's an Orthodox church
located south of Kaha.

00:13:26.490 --> 00:13:30.760
It's a famous cultural landmark
built by digging into a hill.

00:13:31.330 --> 00:13:32.960
The information desk told me

00:13:32.960 --> 00:13:36.770
that a Japanese asked where the
church is located 30 minutes ago.

00:13:36.770 --> 00:13:40.270
Just after that, a Hummer crew,
on their way to occupying Kaha,

00:13:40.270 --> 00:13:44.430
radioed back about a multinational
forces soldier hitching a ride.

00:13:45.610 --> 00:13:48.540
But what if that person wasn't
Captain Gowa?

00:13:49.150 --> 00:13:52.020
You and Captain Gowa are about
the only people on this base

00:13:52.020 --> 00:13:54.380
who can't speak English!

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:58.450
But I don't speak English
so well either.

00:14:03.660 --> 00:14:07.200
Even if Captain Gowa did
head toward Kaha,

00:14:07.200 --> 00:14:08.930
we have no transportation
to get there.

00:14:08.930 --> 00:14:12.490
I thought this might come up so
I've already made preparations.

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:17.640
Wait a minute! How did you
come across this?

00:14:17.640 --> 00:14:20.240
We asked for a little favor.

00:14:20.240 --> 00:14:21.870
Right, Captain Kaburagi?

00:14:42.970 --> 00:14:45.140
Oh, I wish the others
could have seen it.

00:14:45.140 --> 00:14:46.260
Captain Ataka!

00:14:48.000 --> 00:14:52.480
But I wonder why Captain Gowa
wants to go to the church in Kaha?

00:14:52.480 --> 00:14:55.080
Don't ask me. I don't know either.

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:57.750
More importantly, I just heard this.

00:14:57.750 --> 00:15:01.490
Guerrilla activity by the anti-coup
faction has increased a lot

00:15:01.490 --> 00:15:03.490
in the areas around the capital.

00:15:03.490 --> 00:15:07.650
Oh no! If Captain Gowa is walking
around in his uniform...

00:15:08.830 --> 00:15:11.520
There's a good chance he's
become a target for someone.

00:15:12.460 --> 00:15:16.730
What about preparing the
Tactical Armors for transport?

00:15:18.340 --> 00:15:20.900
Right now, our highest priority
is rescuing Captain Gowa.

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:31.430
You're the one!

00:16:52.230 --> 00:16:53.700
Why did you come here?

00:16:56.730 --> 00:16:59.220
You saw it as well, didn't you?

00:17:00.300 --> 00:17:01.790
Saw what?

00:17:07.780 --> 00:17:09.980
Before you said,

00:17:09.980 --> 00:17:11.970
"Don't bring back the terror."

00:17:12.550 --> 00:17:14.350
Bring back what?

00:17:14.350 --> 00:17:16.680
What is this terror you speak of?

00:17:17.190 --> 00:17:21.630
If it's a fate that you can't escape,

00:17:21.630 --> 00:17:25.190
if it's a fate that you can't
change, you can only accept it.

00:17:26.060 --> 00:17:27.220
But that's not true.

00:17:28.470 --> 00:17:30.400
Time is not unchanging.

00:17:30.970 --> 00:17:32.870
Fate is not carved in stone.

00:17:33.700 --> 00:17:36.370
These are the words that
you spoke to me.

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:40.600
I spoke?

00:17:43.910 --> 00:17:46.780
I know this woman.

00:17:47.850 --> 00:17:50.150
I know of her from a
long time ago.

00:17:50.750 --> 00:17:55.320
I know that I've known
this woman!

00:17:58.960 --> 00:18:00.590
But that's impossible!

00:18:06.340 --> 00:18:08.540
No one knows what sentiments

00:18:08.540 --> 00:18:15.410
were entrusted to the icon
when the artist painted it.

00:18:16.080 --> 00:18:23.040
But the sentiments captured here
live on after a thousand years.

00:18:36.430 --> 00:18:37.800
I knew it.

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:39.790
Run!

00:18:46.180 --> 00:18:47.540
Let me go!

00:18:47.540 --> 00:18:49.380
I still have things I
need to ask you.

00:18:57.190 --> 00:18:59.350
Put your hands on top
of your head.

00:19:03.060 --> 00:19:06.630
We've captured the Japanese
invitator who contacted Miharu.

00:19:06.630 --> 00:19:07.650
Symbol?

00:19:12.800 --> 00:19:14.060
Yushiro!

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:25.910
Get in!

00:19:26.580 --> 00:19:28.780
Here we go! Go!

00:19:31.990 --> 00:19:34.260
Pull yourself in! You might
bite your tongue!

00:19:34.260 --> 00:19:35.750
Get down!

00:19:41.830 --> 00:19:43.130
Okay!

00:20:09.930 --> 00:20:12.160
Oh, come on! Get out of my way!

00:20:13.400 --> 00:20:15.030
Who is she?

00:20:15.030 --> 00:20:17.120
Captain, I never guessed it of you.

00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:30.780
Small arms fire isn't
going to stop us!

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:37.180
No way!

00:20:55.040 --> 00:20:57.340
The tires aren't making contact!

00:21:07.150 --> 00:21:08.670
Yushiro!

00:21:16.590 --> 00:21:21.730
Run! Symbol is only after me.
They're not concerned with you.

00:21:21.730 --> 00:21:22.900
Symbol?

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:26.170
They still don't know about you.

00:21:26.170 --> 00:21:27.660
That's why...

00:21:31.740 --> 00:21:34.770
I'm afraid not, my dear Miharu.

00:21:36.280 --> 00:21:39.350
Wait! He has nothing
to do with this!

00:21:39.350 --> 00:21:41.520
Let this person go!

00:21:41.520 --> 00:21:44.920
Unfortunately for you,
we happen to know.

00:22:29.080 --> 00:22:33.900
Hark

00:22:35.060 --> 00:22:40.350
It's time I journey

00:22:43.880 --> 00:22:51.020
Break apart my heart

00:22:51.190 --> 00:22:57.550
For crimson sadness

00:22:57.880 --> 00:23:05.060
Pours out from it

00:23:05.270 --> 00:23:08.980
I can only, oh

00:23:09.090 --> 00:23:12.170
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:12.260 --> 00:23:17.780
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:33.000 --> 00:23:36.880
I can only, oh

00:23:36.970 --> 00:23:40.030
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:40.100 --> 00:23:45.230
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:46.760 --> 00:23:53.210
I beg you, be by my side

00:24:01.090 --> 00:24:03.390
The sun sets on the yellow land.

00:24:04.090 --> 00:24:08.390
A meeting that felt pre-arranged
and prepared has ended.

00:24:09.870 --> 00:24:13.060
I look back, but the darkness
of mystery only thickens.

00:24:14.870 --> 00:24:16.400
You are Miharu

00:24:17.010 --> 00:24:19.240
Feelings for you still linger
as I return home

00:24:19.810 --> 00:24:23.540
Your name now nestled deep down
in the darkness in my heart.

00:24:24.480 --> 00:24:27.280
Farewell battlefields.
